WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.425
Route Operations guides you through a single route day, from import to proof.

2
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:14.850
Begin with the job import template in the Customer Launch Docket.

3
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:22.275
Mandatory fields are customer name and delivery address.

4
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:29.700
Add time windows, service duration, load dimensions, required equipment, driver rules, access instructions, temperature, hazmat, and handling details only if they impact the real route.

5
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.300
Import one representative day and inspect the preview before saving.

6
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.900
Rectify duplicate rows, incomplete addresses, conflicting appointment windows, inconsistent units, and missing routing constraints.

7
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:46.500
After import, open job readiness.

8
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.100
Every pilot job requires a routable pickup or delivery location.

9
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.700
Address missing location data before optimization.

10
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.819
Open Routing and create the route draft.

11
00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:11.938
Verify the intended service date, depot, jobs, vehicles, Drivers, and optimization objective.

12
00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:19.056
Examine every unassigned job and blocker.

13
00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:26.175
Resolve capacity, pallet fit, appointment, equipment, certification, driver, territory, access, temperature, or hazmat conflicts with specific solutions, not silent overrides.

14
00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:32.030
Review optimizer provenance before publication.

15
00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.885
A hosted pilot route must use provider-backed road network inputs.

16
00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:43.740
The system identifies the solver, matrix provider and mode, coverage, solve time, fallback state, and warnings.

17
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.595
A simulated preview or straight line fallback is not acceptable for production readiness evidence.

18
00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:55.450
Rectify the provider or data issue and run the plan again.

19
00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:01.875
When the draft is ready, publish it and open Dispatch.

20
00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:08.300
Assign the trained pilot Driver and eligible vehicle, confirm dispatch readiness, and release the practice route.

21
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:14.725
During execution, monitor stop status, Driver messages, timing, and exceptions.

22
00:02:14.725 --> 00:02:21.150
Keep route changes and decisions within the system to maintain a complete operational record.

23
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:28.094
After the Driver services a stop, open Proof of Delivery.

24
00:02:28.094 --> 00:02:35.038
Confirm the required photo, signature, recipient, note, and timestamps are persisted for that stop.

25
00:02:35.038 --> 00:02:41.981
Resolve every failed or skipped stop with a reason and owner.

26
00:02:41.981 --> 00:02:48.925
The readiness card completes only when the organization has imported jobs, a provider-backed route, a dispatched practice route, and a proof artifact.

27
00:02:48.925 --> 00:02:58.550
Use the practice route as a rehearsal, not a demo shortcut.

28
00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:08.175
Ask the Dispatcher to explain why the route is provider-backed, why each vehicle and Driver are eligible, what the top blocker would look like, and where the final proof appears.

29
00:03:08.175 --> 00:03:17.800
If the explanation relies on a spreadsheet or private text message, move that information into the appropriate system record before considering the route operations track complete.
